---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Updates"
  description="Recent updates to Kreativ Auto, including new guides, better fitment notes, stronger generation hubs, and site improvements."
>
  <div class="container-shell py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="surface p-8 sm:p-10">
      <p class="eyebrow">Updates</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">Recent updates</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-steel">
        A running record of the bigger improvements made to Kreativ Auto as the site gets deeper, clearer, and more useful.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-6">
      <article class="surface p-6 sm:p-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">April 2026</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">From structured site to real editorial property</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-steel marker:text-accent">
          <li>Expanded the Civic, RAV4, and Tiguan clusters with more problem guides, more best-parts guides, and stronger internal linking between diagnosis, parts, and ownership pages.</li>
          <li>Grouped vehicles by generation and facelift so browsing now works at the level where real problem and fitment overlap actually happens.</li>
          <li>Turned the strongest generation pages into better starting points with common trouble spots, first parts to check, trim and year caveats, visual highlights, and clearer next-read paths.</li>
          <li>Built a full guides layer around the three strongest clusters, including common-problems guides, maintenance guides, pre-purchase guides, trim-buying guides, and what-to-avoid guides.</li>
          <li>Added comparison guides for the ownership splits that matter most, including Civic 1.5T vs 2.0, RAV4 Hybrid vs gas, Tiguan FWD vs 4MOTION, and Tiguan pre-facelift vs facelift.</li>
          <li>Improved the strongest problem guides with quick verdicts, first checks, likely confusion points, and clearer signs that a car should not keep being driven.</li>
          <li>Improved the strongest best-parts pages with direct product links, clearer buying tiers, and better “best for” and “avoid if” logic.</li>
          <li>Added more branded and better-matched part imagery, introduced generated thumbnails for faster browsing, and converted heavier hero images to lighter web formats.</li>
          <li>Improved the design system with stronger flagship-page treatment, better typography, denser image coverage, and more editorial hierarchy across the homepage, guides, and generation hubs.</li>
          <li>Added browse filters to the main hub pages so it is easier to narrow the site by cluster, guide type, category, and symptom area.</li>
          <li>Renamed the public changelog to Updates, added a site favicon, and cleaned up more of the public-facing navigation and trust presentation.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="surface p-6 sm:p-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">March 2026</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Launch version</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-steel marker:text-accent">
          <li>Launched the first public version of Kreativ Auto with car pages, problem guides, and best-parts pages for common maintenance and repair decisions.</li>
          <li>Added browsing pages for brands, models, and part categories so it is easier to jump from one vehicle or repair topic to the next.</li>
          <li>Expanded the homepage with featured cars, common problems, and parts guides to help visitors reach useful pages faster.</li>
          <li>Reworked the writing across the site to make problem symptoms, likely causes, and repair options clearer and easier to scan.</li>
          <li>Added real car and parts photos across key pages to make the site feel more visual and easier to browse.</li>
          <li>Published About, Affiliate Disclosure, Editorial Policy, and Contact pages so readers can better understand how recommendations are made.</li>
          <li>Improved search visibility with sitemap support, crawl guidance, breadcrumbs, and structured data.</li>
          <li>Brought the site live on its public domain.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
